  "meteorite":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"I close the meteorite room and try the door across thecorridor.",zh:"我关上陨石房间的门，又打开了走廊对面的门。"},{en:"If the contamination were terrestrial, one could expect equal amounts of the molecules (or less) to be present in the meteorite samples, certainly not more.",zh:"如果污染是来自地面的，在陨石样品中有可能会发现等量（或者较少）的分子，但肯定不会多。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meteoritic":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"Were they meteoritic matter from space, reflected light from polar icebergs or a high-altitude version of lightning?",zh:"它们是太空里的彗星物质、极地冰山反射的光，还是高空的闪电？"},{en:"Scientists think the glass was fused in a meteoritic impact 30 million years ago, making it rare and luminous enough to befit a king.",zh:"科学家认为这种玻璃是由3000万年前的陨石冲击地面融溶而成，它的珍稀和光亮足以适用于国王。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meteoroid":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"Shortly before the uninhabited space station reached orbit in .May 1973,aeroaynamic pressure ripped off a meteoroid and heat shield.",zh:"在1973年5月无人空间站到达轨道前不久，空气动力压力扯破了一个流星体和挡热板。 分析：首先，从逻辑上看，说：“空气动力压力扯破了一个流星体”，是不合事理的，荒谬可笑的。"},{en:"When a meteoroid enters the atmosphere of the earth (becoming a meteor), it is actually the speed compressing the air in front of the object that causes it to heat up.",zh:"流星体闯入地球的大气层（变成流星之前）时，由于高速飞行，它的前端与空气强烈摩擦发热。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meteorological":{collocations:["meteorological data","meteorological station","meteorological observation","meteorological bureau","meteorological satellite","meteorological disaster","meteorological observatory","meteorological element"],examples:[{en:"...adverse meteorological conditions.",zh:"…不利的气象条件。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meteorologist":{collocations:[],examples:[{en:"\"This is probably one of the worst storms since 1990,\" a meteorologist in Seattle said.",zh:"西雅图气象专家表示，这也许是自1990年以来最严重的暴风雪。"},{en:"At the time, he noted that \"One meteorologist remarked that if the theory were correct, one flap of a seagull's wings could change the course of weather forever\".",zh:"在文中，他写道：“一位气象学者注意到，如果这个理论是正确的，那就意味着一只海鸥扇动一下翅膀能够永久地改变天气的进程”。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meteorology":{collocations:["agricultural meteorology","synoptic meteorology"],examples:[{en:"For example geography, meteorology, physics and history.",zh:"例如地理学，气象学，物理（学）和历史。"},{en:"Modern weather forecasts try to take the mystery out of the meteorology.",zh:"现代天气预报试图揭开气象学的神秘面纱。"}],deepExplanation:""},
  "meter":{collocations:["square meter","flow meter","meter reading","water meter","power meter","energy meter","pressure meter","watt-hour meter"],examples:[{en:"The iris of the eye is photographed from up to one meter away.",zh:"眼睛的虹膜最远可在一公尺外的距离接受摄影。"}],deepExplanation:""},
